hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3009","###
 Narrated to us Al-Hasan ibn Qaz'ah, who said: Narrated to us Al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman, who said: Narrated to us Musa ibn 'Uqba, who informed me: Nafi' reported from Ibn 'Umar (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came on the Day of the Conquest riding a camel, with Usama ibn Zayd (RA) riding behind him as his companion, and Bilal (RA) and 'Uthman"
"3010","**
Narrated to us ‘Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-‘Ala’ and Muhammad ibn ‘Umar ibn al-‘Abbas, who said:
Sufyan narrated to us — ‘Abd al-Jabbar said: Ayyub narrated to us, having heard it from Nafi‘, from Ibn ‘Umar.
And Muhammad said: From Ayyub, from Nafi‘, from Ibn ‘Umar, who said:
On the Day of the Conquest, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered Makkah while riding the camel of Usamah. He tethered the camel at the courtyard of the Ka‘bah, then called for the key to be brought from ‘Uthman ibn Talhah. The latter went to his mother, but she refused to give it to him. He said, “Give it to me, or I will draw the sword from my sheath!” So she handed it over to him, and he opened the door. The Prophet (ﷺ) entered, accompanied by ‘Uthman, Bilal, and Usamah. They closed the door for a long while.

Ibn ‘Umar (RA) said:
I was a strong young man, so I outran the others and found Bilal standing at the door. I asked, “Bilal, where did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) pray?”
He replied, “Between the two front pillars.”
I forgot to ask him how many rak‘ahs he prayed.

This is the wording of Muhammad ibn ‘Amr’s hadith."
